U.S. Customs and Border Protection  
National Commodity Specialist Division  
New York, NY

**RE: Request for a binding country of origin ruling — steel brackets**

Dear Sir or Madam:

Pursuant to 19 C.F.R. Part 177, [REQUESTER NAME] respectfully requests a binding ruling on the country of origin of steel brackets for purposes of marking, determined under the Part 102 rules of origin (19 C.F.R. § 102.11, with the tariff shifts of § 102.20).

## Facts

Steel brackets are stamped in Mexico from coil made in China.

## Issue

What is the country of origin of steel brackets, produced as described above, under the Part 102 rules of origin, 19 C.F.R. § 102.11 with the tariff shifts of § 102.20, for purposes of marking?

This request concerns the origin of the merchandise for marking under the Part 102 rules only. It does not ask CBP to decide the country of origin for Section 301 duties, which is a separate question, and the requester does not contend that marking origin settles it.

## Requester's position

The requester submits that the merchandise is a product of Mexico, for marking under the Part 102 rules, based on these key factors: tariff shift met in Mexico. [REQUESTER TO CONFIRM AND EXPAND WITH COUNSEL.]

## Earlier CBP rulings considered

- N340187 ([rulings.cbp.gov](https://rulings.cbp.gov/ruling/N340187)).

